{"abstract":[{"text":"An edge colouring with at most Δ + 1 colours (Vizing’s bound), by Misra and Gries’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"constructive proof. Edges in position order, each coloured through a fan at its end with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"lesser vertex index, every choice the least colour or vertex available. At least Δ colours","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always, and Δ + 1 on class-2 graphs (odd cycles, odd complete graphs, Petersen), but","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"sometimes Δ + 1 on class-1 graphs too (K(4)); on a bipartite graph ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartiteEdgeColoring()"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"always gives Δ. O(m · (Δ² + n)) time: a fan has at most Δ vertices, each found among the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges at u, and a path at most n edges. O(n + m) memory. For a multigraph","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"digraph.undirectedView"},{"text":" with an antiparallel pair is one), use ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"greedyEdgeColoring()"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/coloringmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/edgecoloring()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ColoringModule\/documentation\/ColoringModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/edgeColoring()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":